---
// The small grey label that opens a part of a case study ("Discovery",
// "Design"…), with the line that starts a section under it. It keeps
// --sp-label between that line and whatever follows, whatever gap its parent
// uses: the parent publishes its gap as --gap (see .cs-stack in the page
// styles) and the label makes up the rest.
---

<h2 class="section-label"><slot /></h2>

<style>
  .section-label {
    flex: 1 1 100%;
    margin: 0 0 calc(var(--sp-label) - var(--gap, 0px));
    padding-bottom: 24px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--cs-rule);
    font-family: var(--cs-font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 20px;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--cs-muted);
  }
</style>
